CO2Fix_3_1

450	# simulation lenght [yr]

comments
{
This file is based on the example file with managed Scots pine stand in Finland. Rotation length 90 years.

Scots pine stand in southern Finland, site type VT
Rotation length 90 years

Climate change affecting the increment was taken from the LTEEF study, based on calculation with the FINNFOR model (Kramer and Mohren, 2001). Allocation patterns to other tree compartments are nto changed. Climate data for the soil compartment have been updated, based on the climate scenario underlying the FINNFOR runs.

References:

Koivisto, P. 1959. Growth and yield tables. Communications Instituti Forestalis Fenniae. 51: 1-44. Finnish Forest Research Insitute. Helsinki, Finland. (compilation of Norway spruce, Scots pine, white birch, and common birch treated in different ways )

Marklund, L. G. 1988. Biomassafunktioner för tall, gran och björk I Sverige, Sveriges lantbruksuniversitetet, Rappoter-Skog 45, 1-73.

}

